 "title": "Biofilm Formation and Composition in E. coli and Rhodosporidium babjevae",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the formation and composition of biofilms in E. coli and Rhodosporidium babjevae. E. coli grows into a biofilm, which has curli fibers and curli amyloid fibers as components. Biofilms also have water uptake and influence agar and nutrients. Rhodosporidium babjevae produces EPSs, which have antiproliferative activity and free radical scavenging activity. The cluster also includes various methods and tools used to study and analyze biofilms, such as SDS-PAGE, Curli fiber, and Sigma.",
